## LANGUAGE
Detect the country FIRST from address, coordinates, Maps URL and reviews (English reviews on a Tunisian business do NOT make the site English). The PRIMARY language, default on load and used for all main copy, is the country's business language:
- French: Tunisia, Morocco, Algeria, France, Luxembourg, Switzerland, Senegal, Ivory Coast, Cameroon, Mali, DRC and other francophone countries; Belgium (Dutch if Flanders)
- German: Germany, Austria. Spanish: Spain, Mexico, Argentina, Colombia and other hispanophone countries. Italian: Italy. Portuguese: Portugal, Brazil. Dutch: Netherlands. Turkish: Turkey.
- English: UK, USA, Australia, English-speaking Canada.
- Arabic: UAE, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Kuwait, Bahrain, Oman, Egypt, Jordan; Lebanon (French if the context is French).
- Unsure → language of the reviews.
Optionally add a small AR/EN language switcher in the navbar (hero + contact essentials).

## COPYWRITING
Human, believable, industry-specific, persuasive: storytelling, emotional hooks, sensory wording, strong CTAs. Avoid "Welcome to our website", "We provide quality services", "Customer satisfaction is our priority" and any generic AI copy.

## SECTIONS
Every body section MUST have a unique descriptive id (hero, services, testimonials, about, faq, contact, footer). No anonymous blocks, no ids like "section-1".
1. NAVBAR: as specified above.
2. HERO: unforgettable. Massive headline, emotional subheadline, primary + secondary CTA, rating display, animated layered background. Instantly conveys trust, identity, value.
3. SERVICES: not plain cards. Dynamic alternating layouts, visual storytelling, hover animations.
